\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Positioning of \textsc  {EVIRAG}\xspace  \ relative to the closest neighboring paradigms. \textsc  {EVIRAG}\xspace  \ differs from prior work not only in generating multiple views, but in linking those views to scientific provenance, explicit contradiction structure, causal disagreement attribution, and evidence-conditioned confidence. MADAM-RAG's ``resolves conflict'' entry is correct by design: its Moderator agent produces one synthesized answer, which is appropriate for tasks requiring a single verdict but loses viewpoint structure for tasks requiring human deliberation over contested evidence---the use case \textsc  {EVIRAG}\xspace  \ targets.}}{3}{table.caption.8}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{tab:rw-compare}{{1}{3}{Positioning of \system \ relative to the closest neighboring paradigms. \system \ differs from prior work not only in generating multiple views, but in linking those views to scientific provenance, explicit contradiction structure, causal disagreement attribution, and evidence-conditioned confidence. MADAM-RAG's ``resolves conflict'' entry is correct by design: its Moderator agent produces one synthesized answer, which is appropriate for tasks requiring a single verdict but loses viewpoint structure for tasks requiring human deliberation over contested evidence---the use case \system \ targets}{table.caption.8}{}}
